Package: regmorbidity
Type: Package
Title: Condition Indicators from Danish Register Data with Editable Code Lists
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jie", "Zhang", role = "aut"),
    person("Sara", "Schwartz", email = "saras@clin.au.dk", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: A general approach to deriving condition indicators, with dates,
    from Danish register data. It computes no score and is not an
    implementation of any published index. Conditions are defined in plain CSV
    code lists that users edit, extend and version themselves - one file per
    condition if preferred - rather than in code. Medication (ATC) conditions
    require a configurable number of dispensings within a configurable time
    window, and the onset date is the date of the qualifying dispensing.
    Prefer extracting all conditions in one pass (batch for medications);
    a sequential, one-condition-at-a-time path with disk checkpoints is
    available when the cohort or year range is large or raw events are needed. The code lists distributed with the package take their
    starting point in those used by Prior and colleagues (2016)
    <doi:10.1093/aje/kwv324>, and users are expected to revise the code lists
    for their own study.
